---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CodeExample from "../components/CodeExample.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { SITE } from "../consts";
import { examples } from "../lib/examples";

const functions = examples.find((example) => example.id === "functions");
if (functions === undefined) throw new Error("The functions example is required.");
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Why Kwechiri"
  description="Why Kwechiri is designed as an Igbo-first programming language rather than translated JavaScript."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Language purpose"
    title="A language should fit its community."
    lead="Kwechiri begins from Igbo identity and builds a coherent programming language around it. Translation is not the design model."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Igbo first is a design constraint.</h2>
      <p>
        An Igbo-first language should be readable and teachable for Igbo
        speakers without reducing the engineering quality of the compiler,
        runtime, diagnostics, or tools. Technical correctness matters when
        literal translation and coherent semantics conflict.
      </p>
      <p>
        That means Kwechiri owns its language contract: keywords, expression
        behavior, types, control flow, function semantics, modules, standard
        APIs, errors, and compatibility policy all belong to Kwechiri rather
        than to accidental JavaScript behavior.
      </p>

      <h2>Professional and beginner-friendly are compatible goals.</h2>
      <div class="definition-grid">
        <div class="definition">
          <h3>Clear for learners</h3>
          <p>
            Strict types and located diagnostics help a new programmer
            understand what happened and where.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="definition">
          <h3>Built for real tools</h3>
          <p>
            Explicit compiler stages, tests, versioned specifications, and ADRs
            keep behavior reviewable.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Interoperable without surrendering identity.</h2>
      <p>
        Kwechiri currently compiles to JavaScript and runs on Node.js through an
        explicit runtime boundary. That implementation choice preserves a path
        to modern ecosystems without making JavaScript the language definition.
      </p>

      <CodeExample
        label="Functions"
        code={functions.source}
        output={functions.output}
      />

      <h2>What “active development” means.</h2>
      <p>
        Some language foundations, modules, and the first Standard Library batch
        are certified. Browser execution, VS Code support, final terminology,
        packaging, licensing, and 1.0 compatibility are not complete.
      </p>
      <div class="callout callout--gold">
        <strong>Read the source of truth.</strong>
        The current specification and decision records live in the repository.
        <a href={`${SITE.github}/tree/main/docs`}>Browse the documentation on GitHub</a>.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
